<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fan Shiman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fan Shiman was a king of Funan in the early 3rd century, known from Chinese histories. A general who was raised to the throne, he is said to have built a fleet and subdued more than ten neighbouring states, extending Funan's control over the coasts and trade routes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-thailand">Gulf of Thailand</a> and the Malay peninsula. He is described as the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-king">Great King</a> of Funan'.</p></div>
